# Simulation: Mix two solutions 1:1, then heat from 20°C to 200°C in 10 discrete steps
# Solution 1: 100 mmol/kg dissolved inorganic carbon
# Solution 2: 100 mmol/kg calcium
# After 1:1 mixing: 50 mmol/kg C and 50 mmol/kg Ca in 1 kg water (0.5 kg each)
# Allow calcite to precipitate/dissolve
# 10 steps: 20, 38, 56, 74, 92, 110, 128, 146, 164, 182, 200°C (11 temps, 10 steps)

SOLUTION 1
    temp      20
    pH        7.0
    C(4)      100 mmol/kgw
    units     mmol/kgw

SOLUTION 2
    temp      20
    pH        7.0
    Ca        100 mmol/kgw
    units     mmol/kgw

# Mix 1:1 (0.5 kg each = 1 kg total)
MIX 1
    1   0.5
    2   0.5

EQUILIBRIUM_PHASES 1
    Calcite   0.0   0.0

REACTION_TEMPERATURE 1
    20.0  38.0  56.0  74.0  92.0  110.0  128.0  146.0  164.0  182.0  200.0

SELECTED_OUTPUT
    -file   mixing_heating7.sel
    -reset  false
    -temperature true
    -equilibrium_phases Calcite

END
